  - Execute exactly once after push: two independent full-corpus Chromium profiles, run-1 true worker termination and fresh-worker recovery, zero network/errors, bounded resources, process closure, profile deletion, raw private outputs, and one independent verifier invocation. Never retry or overwrite this registration.
  - Preserve pushed preregistration commit `dc0f5f783de54b8c556064bc1d8a6b21d9cdb9a9`, corpus SHA256 `9503fd6df325f1a46dec56674d2aa72ce225d6bf1c9477abd56bb4542ef99caa`, execution preregistration SHA256 `bccc1631c519774ca46d77100ba59dae0d3eb4dcc681cd227f192bf558319466`, verification preregistration v1 SHA256 `cc1472a7531095323dc1fe2fc2bb878bedfff4cc2cc5b5651f129c4800b0ed05`, and source closure SHA256 `3f97f1a43506f4908c991e85e54ab46e2e92dfd02d3f9aec59453f7dacf6b8b0` unchanged. V1's four outputs and structural verifier failure are terminal evidence, not a parity verdict.
  - Preserve v2 verification preregistration SHA256 `c02523a654c95007b9169bcd4c835b4283f9c7459796d8a943cc4ed0381242b3`, verifier SHA256 `1fac2f476e04b5624fa7030791f5f40faa87d7269a5e215320e1dcab0925f1ad`, and candidate executable SHA256 `1ee0339cecd32cf5651c295b3ead0ff9c612be42fa80bf42e43686804ac480fe`. Their pushed no-output boundary and single completed execution are immutable history.
  - Preserve the exact successful v2 native parity receipt and all four raw outputs unchanged; never rerun, repair, normalize, select, or reinterpret either v1 or v2.
  - Close the remaining Tokenizer2 gate with a separately preregistered real-Chromium full-artifact WASM replay, cancellation and repeated-use checks, privacy assertions, and bounded load/memory/throughput measurements before Template2 consumes the accepted identity.
  - Preserve implementation commit `80f199d51f49417a699c57743550bf81153fa6e6`, runtime-vector SHA256 `c7a0fdaf1dd578928e6a438be308dad5a9e8cc10e2bbb6da4b2c5e10bebe71f1`, canonical artifact SHA256 `c010e2818c64713310699e9ad928d3b22cfeb004756ae8e03acaaee5897e613a`, and independent Node oracle SHA256 `df0b51548dce1a7174166479504a35fe6f5b256dd3168cae970ac8c1df7257b9` as the exact canonical-fixture scalar/WASM foundation; do not rerun it without invalidation.
  - After the full Tokenizer2 gate closes, implement exact publisher chat-template vectors plus deterministic seeded sampling before calling native/WASM text generation conformant.
  - Replace the conformance-only embedded-fixture boundary with a bounded production large-model ownership/transfer ABI, then implement the truthful P2P-first or local-conversion browser lifecycle without text/script handoffs.
  - Preserve implementation commit `09c0e2bc96d728f220b322fbe9d33774f8664b1e`, trainer SHA256 `aded5f91db040008685a506e6a59e09593b68bdb69688095fa0aef8db8e0c50b`, and environment-lock-v3 SHA256 `68c36c8492c59c0006e3bfa018b0d84dbc1832379733512c4e979b9a17ac49eb` as the exact non-authorizing trainer foundation.
  - Obtain two genuinely separate completed `holdout-custody-v6` contributions. Never author or sign either contribution as this agent.
  - Materialize the exact 1,024-record pilot curriculum and complete teacher, license, PII, malicious-artifact, and removal lineage outside Git.
  - Obtain two complete record-ordered primary review ledgers under distinct reviewer identities and custody domains; use a third distinct adjudicator only for actual disagreement.
  - Assemble and seal holdouts create-only, then pass exact lexical, n-gram, entity, template, answer, tombstone, and complete blinded semantic contamination gates.
  - Freeze one exact training lock only after the control program reopens every source, review, holdout, audit, environment, trainer, recipe, stop-rule, and output-root input.
  - Run one deterministic CPU pilot, preserve every checkpoint and terminal result, and merge only an eligible final adapter into a new cryptographically identified source artifact.
  - Run untouched behavioral screening before deterministic sole-SLM2 conversion, then establish scalar/native and browser-WASM conformance before acquisition and browser promotion.
immutable_evidence:
  - The ExactFlat sealed baseline passed only its bounded numerical, controlled-memory, and registered process-crash gates. It is not semantic-memory or product evidence.
  - The frozen TurboVec 0.9.0 four-bit native reference arm is terminally unqualified. Never rerun it, alter its thresholds, or repair its failed process into a pass.
  - Any future compressed-vector arm requires a new preregistration and append-only partial child-process evidence before nonzero-exit rejection.
  - No local fixture, public contract document, or report satisfies authorized MemoryEndpoints individual-account continuity.
engineering_rules:
  - TinyRustLM is pre-release; incur no technical debt and provide no legacy or backward-compatibility support.
  - Rewrite cleanly, remove superseded implementation after verification, and preserve immutable receipts as audit evidence only.
  - Preserve raw failures, fixed seeds, exact identities, bounded allocations, untouched model outputs, and explicit external blockers.
  - Keep static model weights, online KV cache state, durable retrieval vectors, composition graphs, and specialist overlays as separate identity and byte-accounting domains.
  - Do not weaken tests, fabricate live evidence, infer publication from package creation, or infer public reachability from local probes.
  - Keep marketing, documentation, version, release date, last-publish metadata, and per-site update logs synchronized with every stable publication.
next_steps:
  - Complete affected Rust, Node, Chromium, formatting, preregistration, JSON, documentation, UAI, diff, source-identity, and private-input gates while the registered output root remains absent.
  - Commit and push this no-output browser preregistration checkpoint; fetch and prove local HEAD, tracking ref, FETCH_HEAD, and fresh remote are exact; then rehash every input and reprove output-root absence.
  - Execute only the registered two browser observations and one verifier invocation. Preserve its exact terminal result; if it rejects, archive the failure and add only a general regression in a later source commit before a new append-only preregistration.
  - Treat missing genuine holdout authors or curriculum reviewers as explicit external blockers; continue only independent engineering work that cannot forge or weaken those gates.
  - Validate every received contribution against the exact current profile, program, identity, custody, order, factor-diversity, overlap, and bounded-storage contracts before assembly.
  - Materialize and review the curriculum without exposing private records in Git or public receipts, then run all contamination controls and preserve every rejection and tombstone.
  - Verify the exact training lock and run the pinned trainer only after `training_authority` is explicitly granted by the current control program.
  - Preserve raw outputs and exact identities through merge, untouched screen, SLM2 conversion, scalar/WASM parity, acquisition, clean-profile browser conversation, privacy scan, and receipts.
  - Run focused tests after each change and complete affected release gates before deployment; commit and push every coherent green major change immediately.
success_criteria:
  - One cryptographically identified derivative has acceptable provenance and passes the preregistered untouched behavioral screen without repair, retry selection, best-of-N, or answer injection.
  - Its exact source, tokenizer, chat template, training data and reviews, adapter, merged bytes, converter, SLM2 output, runtime, WASM, acquisition, and browser receipts form one content-addressed evidence graph.
  - Conversion is deterministic and produces only canonical SLM2; unsupported or ambiguous tensors fail closed and no SLM1 reader, compatibility alias, migration, repair, or fallback exists.
  - Scalar native inference is the reference and browser WASM conforms for identical model bytes, prompts, tokens, sampling profiles, seeds, KV-cache state, stop conditions, and bounded malformed inputs.
  - The browser acquires a verified P2P artifact when available or performs explicit local conversion when unavailable; it never downloads text or scripts as a substitute.
  - A fresh browser profile completes genuine multi-turn local chat with one rendering per answer, truthful cancellation/restart behavior, no prompt or model upload, and deletion/privacy evidence.
  - Complete affected tests pass, source and UAI memory are committed and pushed, documentation and release history are synchronized, deployment occurs only after full gates, and no campaign claim exceeds live receipts.
